1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--listen-looping","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/listen-looping","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/listen-looping","sourceHash":"b84302eb85a575a7739d0303f419c922de848eb5dc7c7e6d71ec052234964f08","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:53:20.287Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Listen Looping","zh":"循环听辨"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Listen looping is a simple technique: find a section of audio that's hard to understand, and loop it — play it over and over — until you can hear what's being said.","zh":"循环听辨是一种简单的技巧：找出一段难以理解的音频，然后循环播放——一遍又一遍地听——直到你能听清说了什么。"}},{"id":"how-to-do-it","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How to Do It","zh":"如何练习"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"en":"Load audio into a tool like Audacity or <a href=\"https://chorusing.app/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">chorusing.app</a>","zh":"将音频加载到 Audacity 或 <a href=\"https://chorusing.app/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">chorusing.app</a> 之类的工具中"},{"en":"Listen normally and find a section you can't quite understand but think you <em>should</em> be able to","zh":"正常听音频，找出一段你听不太懂、但觉得自己<em>应该</em>能听懂的内容"},{"en":"Select that section and put it on loop","zh":"选中这段内容并将其设为循环播放"},{"en":"Listen repeatedly, focusing on the specific words and sounds","zh":"反复聆听，专注于具体的词语和声音"},{"en":"Once you can hear exactly what's being said, move on","zh":"能准确听清说了什么之后，就继续下一段"}]},{"id":"why-it-works","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It Works","zh":"为什么有效"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"In natural speech, words blend together, sounds get dropped, and familiar words become unrecognizable at full speed. Your brain needs repeated exposure to learn how to parse these fast, connected sounds.","zh":"在自然语流中，单词会连在一起，声音会被省略，熟悉的词在全速播放时也可能变得难以辨认。你的大脑需要反复接触，才能学会解析这些快速且连贯的声音。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Looping gives your ears multiple chances to decode the same section, building the connection between what you hear and what you know.","zh":"循环播放让你的耳朵有多次机会解码同一段内容，从而建立听到的声音与已掌握知识之间的联系。"}},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"技巧"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Skip sections where you don't know the words — looping won't help if the vocabulary is unknown. Focus on sections where you <em>know</em> (or think you know) the words but can't <em>hear</em> them.","zh":"跳过那些含有生词的部分——如果词汇本身不认识，循环播放也无济于事。应专注于那些你<em>认识</em>（或自认为认识）其中的词、却无法把它们<em>听出来</em>的部分。"},{"en":"If available, check a transcript after you've tried to figure it out on your own (this is basically the same as Intensive Listening)","zh":"如果有文本稿，请先尝试自己听懂，再对照查看（这基本上与精听相同）"},{"en":"For an additional challenge, try <a href=\"/roadmap/library/transcription\">Transcription</a>","zh":"想增加难度，可以尝试<a href=\"/roadmap/library/transcription\">听写</a>"}]},{"id":"when-to-use-it","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Use It","zh":"何时使用"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Listen looping is introduced in Phase 3C and continues to be useful through Phase 6.","zh":"循环听辨会在阶段 3C 引入，并会一直到阶段 6 都很有用。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
